{
  "name": "decimal",
  "description": "IEEE 754 decimal128 arithmetic beyond the operators.  `d128` is decimal floating point with 34 significant digits, so a value prints as exactly what it holds: `0.1d 0.2d +` is `0.3`. The operators `+ - * /`, `neg` and the comparisons work on d128 directly; this module has the rest of what IEEE 754-2008 asks of a decimal format, and the elementary functions.  Every result is rounded to 34 digits with roundTiesToEven. `sqrt`, `exp`, `ln` and `log10` are correctly rounded, as is `fma`, which rounds once for the product and the sum. The trigonometric functions carry ten guard digits and reduce their argument against 6400 digits of pi, so `sin` of 1e6144 is as accurate as `sin` of 1.  Decimal values keep the exponent they were written or computed with, so `1.10d` and `1.1d` are equal but print differently; `reduce` strips trailing zeros and `quantize` sets them.",
  "constants": [

  ],
